BlockOptionalMeta's loot-table stub level no longer keeps a Minecraft client reference (it reports the vanilla feature set).
Block drops are rolled on a real ServerLevel and the server's own loot registries, supplied by the host through
HostEnvironment.setLootLevel(). Without one the drops of a block are unknown (logged once, empty): the upstream fallback, a
private level that reloads all data-pack registries, wedges a running Fabric server, so it is never used.

